[gd_scene load_steps=6 format=3]

; Moves one variable: `use_texture_padding`. Each layer tiles the red and yellow quadrants of one
; atlas whose neighbours are green and blue. Godot samples a padded tile from a copy of the atlas
; with the tile's own edge repeated around it, so a linear filter never reads the neighbour. Left:
; padded, linear. Middle: unpadded, linear, where Godot itself bleeds the neighbour into each seam.
; Right: padded, nearest. No other golden draws an adjacent linear-filtered atlas neighbour.

